{"uid":"86fd34a8ddff6d2c","name":"test_two_fast_navigations_leave_exactly_one_refresh_loop","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_refresh_loop#test_two_fast_navigations_leave_exactly_one_refresh_loop","historyId":"6879c7c683db5f5ad1a89b01ee39c66b","time":{"start":1791895691712,"stop":1791895703449,"duration":11737},"description":"Targets the fix in `router()`/`renderRunList` that only installs the\n    refresh timer for the render that is still current when its initial\n    `load()` resolves (`if (myGen === renderGeneration) refreshTimer =\n    startRefreshLoop(load);`). Before task 016, `router()` cleared\n    `refreshTimer` unconditionally on every navigation but a render only\n    *assigned* `refreshTimer` after its own `await load()` -- so a second\n    navigation landing before the first's initial load resolved cleared a\n    variable that was still `null`, and the first render's later,\n    now-superseded `await load()` went on to unconditionally overwrite\n    `refreshTimer` with a brand new interval, orphaning whatever the second\n    render had already installed. Reverting just that one `if` guard back to\n    an unconditional assignment makes this test observe `2` live loops\n    instead of `1` (the orphaned one plus the new one), while every other\n    part of the task 016 diff stays in place.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Targets the fix in <code>router()</code>/<code>renderRunList</code> that only installs the<br />\nrefresh timer for the render that is still current when its initial<br />\n<code>load()</code> resolves (<code>if (myGen === renderGeneration) refreshTimer = startRefreshLoop(load);</code>). Before task 016, <code>router()</code> cleared<br />\n<code>refreshTimer</code> unconditionally on every navigation but a render only<br />\n<em>assigned</em> <code>refreshTimer</code> after its own <code>await load()</code> -- so a second<br />\nnavigation landing before the first's initial load resolved cleared a<br />\nvariable that was still <code>null</code>, and the first render's later,<br />\nnow-superseded <code>await load()</code> went on to unconditionally overwrite<br />\n<code>refreshTimer</code> with a brand new interval, orphaning whatever the second<br />\nrender had already installed. Reverting just that one <code>if</code> guard back to<br />\nan unconditional assignment makes this test observe <code>2</code> live loops<br />\ninstead of <code>1</code> (the orphaned one plus the new one), while every other<br />\npart of the task 016 diff stays in place.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791894578879,"stop":1791894578879,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791894578879,"stop":1791894578879,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791895691708,"stop":1791895691709,"duration":1},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791895691708,"stop":1791895691708,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_task_record_dir","time":{"start":1791895691709,"stop":1791895691709,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attac